            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this salad for a family birthday party and it was a HUGE hit! I added some grated carrots to the recipe and it was a great compliment to the other veggies. Also I cut the tomatoes into quarters and it added lots of colour to the salad. My mom said she will never be able to buy macaroni salad again from a store again."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Melnal"
            },
            "reviewBody": "BEST Macaroni Salad EVER! I added some shelled sunflower seeds (because I had some and needed to use them). I let it set in the fridge overnight and it seemed a little dry so I added a generous spoonful of mayo and stirred it up. LOVED it! Oh, and I also didn't have any beaumonde seasoning, so I used Penzey's Pasta Sprinkle - 1 tsp for every 2 servings. I put in 6 tsp for the full recipe. I'm making a double-batch for the pot-luck Labor Day party!",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-31T22:48:50.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Overall, this turned out well. It's a nice mix of ingredients. I liked the cheddar cheese. I would cut the mayo down to ¾ cup next time, but that's personal preference. I used red and yellow pepper instead of green and didn't realize I was out of tomatoes. It's a nice side dish.",
            "datePublished": "2023-06-26T23:20:07.032Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephanie6962"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I will be making this tonight. I had never heard of Beau Monde, so I looked it up. Got a recipe too. I think I will make mine. Here is the one that I found. Recipe for Beau Monde Seasoning Salt: 1 tablespoon ground cloves 1 1/4 teaspoons ground cinnamon 1 tablespoon salt 1 tablespoon ground bay leaf 1 tablespoon ground allspice 2 tablespoons ground pepper 1 tablespoon ground white pepper 1 teaspoon ground nutmeg 1 teaspoon ground mace 1 teaspoon celery seed In a small mixing bowl, mix together all ingredients. Pour into a tightly closed jar and store in a cool, dry place. Yields approximately 9 tablespoons. With all the great reviews, I can't wait.",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-26T09:38:12.177Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rls"
            },
            "reviewBody": "EXCELLENT SALAD! I omitted the green onions and added 3 Tlbs. sugar. Agree with other reviewers that finely grated carrots is another great add-in, as well as handful of frozen (thawed) peas. If you don't have cherry tomatoes, diced tomatoes work just fine.",
            "datePublished": "2015-05-15T07:25:03.507Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rachel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't use green bell pepper, I used olive oil mayo, I used apple cider vinegar, I put diced jalapeños &amp; diced white onion in it, and I made my own version of beau monde seasoning. I only changed it so much due to lack of ingredients, and/or preference. It turned out awesome! SPICY, but I love spicy.",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-30T19:41:12.270Z"
          },
